        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/memory-safety-oob-read-from-wire-controlled-option-value-index-arithmetic",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Memory safety (OOB read from wire-controlled option value / index arithmetic) — Ruled out: src/coap_debug.c coap_show_pdu COAP_OPTION_OSCORE sub-field printing (lines 994-1054)\n\nResolved dynamically rather than by hand-derivation only. I drove the OSCORE sub-field printer at src/coap_debug.c:994-1054 through the real parse path by sending 91 crafted CoAP options 9 (OSCORE) in request PDUs to a local ASAN+UBSAN coap-server running at debug log level (so coap_show_pdu executes): first byte b0 in {00,01,07,08,09,0F,10,18,20,28,30,38,3F} crossed with tails of length 0,1,2,4,255 including kid-context length prefixes of 0x00/0x05/0xFF, which is what selects the Group-flag, pIV, kid-context and kid branches. No ASAN/UBSAN report and the server stayed alive; 514 additional show_pdu probes and a 240 s libFuzzer run of a harness that parses then calls coap_show_pdu at COAP_LOG_DEBUG were also clean. Bounds control: option length for option 9 is capped at 255 by coap_pdu_parse_opt_base (src/coap_pdu.c:1338), pIV requires cnt <= opt_len-1 with ofs=1, kid-context requires ofs < opt_len and cnt <= opt_len-ofs-1 before ofs++, and kid takes cnt = opt_len-ofs after an ofs >= opt_len check, so every opt_val[ofs+i] read is inside the option value."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/coap_debug.c coap_show_pdu COAP_OPTION_OSCORE sub-field printing (lines 994-1054)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
