        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/stack-buffer-overflow-in-diagnostic-formatting",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stack buffer overflow in diagnostic formatting — Ruled out: src/coap_debug.c coap_snprintf / print_readable / binary payload dump (lines 191-252, 1150-1200)\n\ncoap_snprintf (src/coap_debug.c:229-252) truncates correctly (`*offset = buf_size-1`, early return when start>=buf_size-1) and print_readable (191-227) keeps one spare byte in both the printable (cnt+1<buflen) and escaped (cnt+4<buflen) branches; the binary hex/ascii dump and the readable-payload branch both re-anchor outbuflen and reserve headroom. No caller passes an offset >= buf_size."
          },
