        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/heap-overflow-in-block-wise-reassembly-offset-len-arithmetic-from-block1-fields-and-size1",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Heap overflow in block-wise reassembly (offset/len arithmetic from Block1 fields and SIZE1) — Requires further review: src/coap_block.c lg_srcv Block1 reassembly + coap_block_build_body_lkd (3691-3870, 4589-4630)\n\ncoap_block_build_body_lkd has the SIZE_MAX-8 overflow test, the caller rejects `total_len_set && offset+length > total_len` (src/coap_block.c:3752) and the fast memcpy requires body_data->length >= total, otherwise it resizes to offset+length first. Gap: the multi-iteration BERT walk at 3795-3818 recomputes offset = block.num << (block.szx+4) from wire values; only stateless fuzzing (block/block_check targets, 40k execs) was done, no stateful interleaved Block1 sequences with changing SZX/BERT."
          },
