        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/memory-safety-in-websocket-upgrade-frame-parsing-mask-handling-64-bit-lengths",
          "ruleIndex": 8,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Memory safety in WebSocket upgrade/frame parsing (mask handling, 64-bit lengths) — Ruled out: src/coap_ws.c coap_ws_rd_http_header / coap_ws_read / coap_ws_build_key_hash (385-780)\n\nResolved by bounds proof plus directed fuzzing/live testing. Correction to the earlier note: rd_header is 14 bytes (COAP_MAX_FS = 2+8+4, include/coap3/coap_ws_internal.h:34), not 128, so I re-derived every access. Control 1: the mask-key copy at src/coap_ws.c:658 uses offset 2+extra_hdr_len with extra_hdr_len <= 8 (len==127) before the +4, i.e. at most &rd_header[10]..[13], inside the 14-byte array. Control 2: src/coap_ws.c:661 returns before any use when hdr_ofs < 2+extra_hdr_len, so a partial header never reaches the copy sites. Control 3: in the leftover branch src/coap_ws.c:742-751, bytes_size < ret = hdr_ofs-2-extra, so source 2+extra+bytes_size < hdr_ofs <= 14 and source+len == hdr_ofs, keeping both memcpy and memmove inside rd_header. Control 4: src/coap_ws.c:698 rejects (size_t)bytes_size > datalen before any payload copy, and a 64-bit length >= 2^63 becomes a negative ssize_t that this cast turns into a huge size and rejects. Control 5: coap_ws_rd_http_header caps http_ofs at 159 and each read at 14 bytes, so the post-blank-line remainder copied into rd_header[14] at src/coap_ws.c:559 is <= 13 (verified from the live read pattern: handshake arrives in 14-byte reads). Evidence: 1,449,089 libFuzzer execs of a WS-layer harness (persistent context, modes: HTTP upgrade, post-handshake frames, write path) with ASAN+UBSAN, zero reports; 14 crafted frame probes (masked/unmasked, 7/16/64-bit lengths incl. 0xFFFFFFFF and 2^64-1, close/ping opcodes, declared length > datalen) and 54 split/coalesced delivery probes (every byte-boundary split, two-three frames in one segment, header-only then payload) against a local ASAN coap-server, all clean. Residual: only an uninitialised read of rd_header bytes 10-13 when a 127-length header is still partial; it is discarded and re-copied on the next read, so it is not a memory-safety issue."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/coap_ws.c coap_ws_rd_http_header / coap_ws_read / coap_ws_build_key_hash (385-780)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Memory safety in WebSocket upgrade/frame parsing (mask handling, 64-bit lengths)",
              "surface": "src/coap_ws.c coap_ws_rd_http_header / coap_ws_read / coap_ws_build_key_hash (385-780)",
              "recorded_by": "PDU Parser Memory Safety",
