            "text": "Buffer overflow / path traversal semantics in URI parsing and URI-* option reassembly — Ruled out: src/coap_uri.c coap_split_uri_sub / coap_check_dots / coap_get_query / coap_get_uri_path (81-350, 675-715, 1111-1300)\n\ncoap_split_uri_sub only produces pointers/lengths into the caller's string (no copies); host is rejected >255 bytes, port parsing is bounded by UINT16_MAX, coap_check_dots handles \"..\",\"%2e%2e\" correctly. coap_get_query/coap_get_uri_path allocate coap_new_string(computed_len) and write exactly computed_len bytes (encoded bytes + nopts-1 separators), verified per-branch; the uint16_t seg_len truncation is unreachable for parsed PDUs because the option parser caps URI-Path/URI-Query at 255. Fuzzed via split_uri/uri_extended (280k+) and pdu_parse_*."
