        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/heap-overflow-when-adding-inserting-updating-removing-options-on-attacker-influenced-pdus",
          "ruleIndex": 11,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Heap overflow when adding/inserting/updating/removing options on attacker-influenced PDUs — Ruled out: src/coap_pdu.c option mutation path (340-390, 550-640, 693-800, 812-860, 869-940)\n\nEvery memmove in coap_remove_option/coap_insert_option/coap_update_option/coap_add_option_internal is sized as used_size - (option - token) [- shrink] and follows a coap_pdu_check_resize() on the same new size; coap_pdu_resize refuses new_size > max_size when max_size is set. Only logic quirk found is the RFC 8768 default Hop-Limit value being COAP_OPTION_HOP_LIMIT (252) at coap_pdu.c:889-895 — not attacker-controlled, matches upstream, reported as an observation only."
