        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/stack-buffer-overflow-via-token-length-in-the-client-fetch-observe-block-path",
          "ruleIndex": 26,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stack buffer overflow via token length in the client FETCH/Observe block path — Ruled out: src/coap_block.c:4351 (track_fetch_observe token copy) and src/coap_net.c extended-token handling\n\nCandidate: src/coap_block.c:4351 memcpy(buf[8], new_token->s, len) where len is lg_crcv->obs_token[n]->length. Traced the origin of obs_token: track_fetch_observe() stores pdu->actual_token (the client's own outgoing token), and the only other caller passes a token from coap_encode_var_safe8() (<=8). Outgoing client tokens come from coap_session_new_token() (uint64 -> <=8 bytes) or from the application; coap_send_lkd() rejects any request whose token exceeds session->max_token_size (src/coap_net.c:1754), which defaults to COAP_TOKEN_DEFAULT_MAX=8 (src/coap_net.c:815) and can only be raised by the application via coap_context_set_max_token_size(). A remote server cannot set the client's token length (it only negotiates support via CSM), so len>8 requires an application that opts into >8-byte tokens and uses a block-wise FETCH with Observe - an operator-controlled precondition, not a remote attacker capability."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/coap_block.c:4351 (track_fetch_observe token copy) and src/coap_net.c extended-token handling"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Stack buffer overflow via token length in the client FETCH/Observe block path",
              "surface": "src/coap_block.c:4351 (track_fetch_observe token copy) and src/coap_net.c extended-token handling",
              "recorded_by": "Block/Session/Observe Audit",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/integer-overflow-truncation-in-stream-framing-length-size-t-vs-uint64-leading-to-short-allocation",
          "ruleIndex": 27,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Integer overflow/truncation in stream framing length (size_t vs uint64) leading to short allocation — Ruled out: src/coap_pdu.c coap_pdu_parse_size (TCP/TLS stream length arithmetic, 1112-1174) fed by src/coap_net.c coap_read_session\n\nControls: coap_pdu_parse_header_size() > length is rejected first (src/coap_pdu.c:1121); each Len/E/TKL form is only read after `length >= 2+extra_for_tkl` / `>= 3+extra_for_tkl` / `>= 5+extra_for_tkl` (1139-1162); TKL > 14 returns 0 (1134); the accumulator is uint64_t and is clamped to (size_t)-1 before the cast (1170-1173); the caller then rejects size > csm_max_message_size (src/coap_net.c:2858) and only after that allocates with coap_pdu_init(coap_session_max_pdu_rcv_size) + coap_pdu_resize(size), whose capacity is alloc_size + max_hdr_size with max_hdr_size = 6 in this build (src/coap_pdu.c:346, include/coap3/coap_pdu_internal.h:113), so T = size + hdr_size always fits; the body copy is additionally guarded by n > alloc_size + hdr_size - partial_read (src/coap_net.c:2805-2813). Verified live: 40+ TCP probes covering Len 0-12 exact/short/long, 8/16/32-bit extended lengths (0, 1, 255, 0xFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF) and TKL 13/14/15 extended-token frames, plus 54 split-delivery probes that split every message at every byte boundary, dribble one byte at a time and coalesce two PDUs in one segment - all against a local ASAN+UBSAN coap-server, no report."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/coap_pdu.c coap_pdu_parse_size (TCP/TLS stream length arithmetic, 1112-1174) fed by src/coap_net.c coap_read_session"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Integer overflow/truncation in stream framing length (size_t vs uint64) leading to short allocation",
              "surface": "src/coap_pdu.c coap_pdu_parse_size (TCP/TLS stream length arithmetic, 1112-1174) fed by src/coap_net.c coap_read_session",
