        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/stack-buffer-overflow-in-the-malformed-option-diagnostic-dump",
          "ruleIndex": 28,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stack buffer overflow in the malformed-option diagnostic dump — Ruled out: src/coap_pdu.c coap_pdu_parse_opt error-dump block (write_prefix/write_char, static outbuf[COAP_DEBUG_BUF_SIZE], 1436-1580)\n\nThe dump runs on any PDU that reached the option loop with a bad option value/length, i.e. directly attacker-triggerable. Controls: write_prefix (src/coap_pdu.c:1436) returns without copying unless *len >= prflen+1, and write_char (1444) requires *len >= 3 and decrements by exactly 2, so obp can never pass outbuf+sizeof-1; the terminating *obp = '\\000' at 1571 is therefore in bounds even when the buffer is full. The tlen loop that copies the offending raw option bytes (1558-1566) stops writing as soon as ok becomes 0 (short-circuit), and when optsize==0 the code sets opt = token+used_size/length=0 before the loop, so the source range is always inside the PDU. Verified: 514 crafted option/delta/length PDUs and 60,000 mutated datagrams against a local ASAN+UBSAN coap-server, which produced hundreds of \"malformed option\" dumps in the log (e.g. \"O: *edfef2...\") with no ASAN report; libFuzzer on pdu_parse_udp (1,000,567 execs) plus the invariant oracle (2.4M parses) also clean."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/coap_pdu.c coap_pdu_parse_opt error-dump block (write_prefix/write_char, static outbuf[COAP_DEBUG_BUF_SIZE], 1436-1580)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Stack buffer overflow in the malformed-option diagnostic dump",
              "surface": "src/coap_pdu.c coap_pdu_parse_opt error-dump block (write_prefix/write_char, static outbuf[COAP_DEBUG_BUF_SIZE], 1436-1580)",
