        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/out-of-bounds-read-write-missing-nul-termination-ipv6-bracket-handling-255-byte-host-limit-port-overflow-return-code-handling",
          "ruleIndex": 31,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Out-of-bounds read/write, missing NUL termination, IPv6 bracket handling, 255-byte host limit, port overflow, return-code handling — No issue identified: src/coap_uri.c: coap_split_uri / coap_split_proxy_uri (host, port, path, query split)\n\nLine-by-line review against RFC 3986/7252 semantics: every pointer advance is bounded by the remaining length, the bracket branch requires a closing ']' and rejects empty hosts, both host branches cap at 255 chars, and the port accumulator cannot overflow because the loop stops as soon as the value exceeds UINT16_MAX. Dynamically: 240k randomized inputs through tests/oss-fuzz/uri_extended_target.c plus 60k structured URI seeds under ASAN/UBSAN with no diagnostic; boundary cases exercised explicitly (60KB hosts in both bracket forms → -6, 60KB port digit string → -4, many-colons → -1, empty host → -3, >=65536 → -4); the project's 201 unit tests pass."
