          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/heap-out-of-bounds-write-on-proxy-entry-allocation-off-by-one",
          "ruleIndex": 36,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Heap out-of-bounds write on proxy entry allocation (off-by-one) — Ruled out: src/coap_proxy.c: coap_proxy_get_add_list_entry (proxy_list realloc + returned entry pointer)\n\nSuspected an off-by-one: `context->proxy_list_count++; return &proxy_list[proxy_list_count];` looks like it returns one element past the allocation. Ruled out: `proxy_list_count` inside the function is a local copy taken before the increment, so the increment only updates the context field and the returned address is exactly the slot that was just zeroed, populated and counted. Confirmed with an instrumented build of the function (prints ret == list base and count field == 1 for the first entry) and with a driver that compares the returned pointer to context->proxy_list and reads a correct uri.host/uri.port through it; thousands of entry creations under ASAN produced no diagnostic."
