            "text": "Use-after-free / dangling session pointer during proxy cleanup — Requires further review: src/coap_proxy.c: proxy request cleanup at context teardown (coap_proxy_cleanup_entry)\n\nConfirmed under ASAN but deliberately not filed (full trace in shared note): coap_free_context() releases sessions (coap_net.c:909) before coap_proxy_cleanup() (coap_net.c:945), so coap_proxy_cleanup_entry→coap_proxy_del_req→coap_proxy_log_entry() reads freed memory via coap_session_get_addr_remote() (heap-use-after-free READ of size 2 at coap_debug.c:274). Trigger requires COAP_LOG_DEBUG plus a pending proxy request at context teardown; an attacker cannot force teardown or change the log level, so no security impact was demonstrated and no CVSS-bearing report was justified — orchestrator decision whether to file it as hardening."
