            "text": "buffer overflow / out-of-bounds read-write in attacker-controlled PDU rendering — No issue identified: src/coap_debug.c diagnostic buffers (coap_show_pdu, print_readable, print_content_format, coap_snprintf)\n\nStatic bound proof plus ASAN/UBSAN validation found no residual defect. Each write is bounded: coap_snprintf() clamps the offset to buf_size-1 and returns only bytes actually written (verified exhaustively for buf_size 1..300 at every valid offset, no canary write past the buffer); print_readable() reserves the NUL and returns <= buflen-1; outbuflen/buf_len are re-derived from strlen() on every branch and buf_len is reset per option, so the \"%.*s\" precision can never exceed the NUL-terminated content of buf. Hostile-PDU harness: 65804-byte extended-length unknown options, 1000-option lists, max-length Proxy-Uri/OSCORE kid+kid-context (including internally inconsistent kid/pIV lengths), 70KB text/binary payloads, CSM/Release/Abort signalling, TCP extended tokens (13/14 nibble). libFuzzer over parse+coap_show_pdu at COAP_LOG_DEBUG: 159,451 runs / 116,993 formatter calls on the default 2056-byte buffer and 622,050 runs / 431,512 formatter calls on a 32-byte buffer build, all clean (output capped at buf_size-1 exactly). Project testdriver: 240/240 pass including the new t_parse_pdu18."
