        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/aead-tag-verification-nonce-reuse-key-derivation-correctness-rfc-8613-rfc-8152-semantics",
          "ruleIndex": 41,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "AEAD tag verification, nonce reuse, key derivation correctness (RFC 8613 / RFC 8152 semantics) — No issue identified: src/oscore/oscore_cose.c + src/oscore/oscore_crypto.c (COSE Encrypt0, HKDF, AEAD wrapper)\n\nBuilt the shipped tests/test_oscore.c against an ASAN+UBSAN build (CUnit) and ran all 37 tests: 37 passed, 389 asserts, 0 failures. This covers the RFC 8613 Appendix C vectors end to end (C.1.1-C.8.2: sender/recipient key and common-IV derivation, sender/recipient nonce for both request and response, external AAD/COSE AAD bytes, and full request/response encrypt/decrypt), so key derivation, nonce construction, AAD composition and tag handling match the RFC for the shipped algorithms. Additionally cross-checked libcoap's ciphertext against an independent Python HKDF-SHA256 + AES-CCM implementation: the captured client request and server response both decrypt with RFC-derived keys/nonce/AAD. Code review of cose_encrypt0_decrypt/encrypt found the length guards correct (ciphertext < tag_len rejected, ciphertext > plaintext+tag_len rejected, key/nonce length checked against the algorithm)."
          },
