        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/replay-window-off-by-one-nonce-reuse-across-messages",
          "ruleIndex": 42,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Replay-window off-by-one / nonce reuse across messages — No issue identified: src/oscore/oscore.c (oscore_generate_nonce, oscore_validate_sender_seq, oscore_increment/roll_back)\n\nReviewed oscore_generate_nonce (S | ID_PIV(7, right aligned) | PIV(5, right aligned), XOR common IV), oscore_increment_sender_seq, oscore_validate_sender_seq and oscore_roll_back_seq against RFC 8613 §5.2/B.1.1. Nonce layout confirmed against an independent implementation and the RFC Appendix C vectors. Live tests with an independent OSCORE peer against a local interop server: a valid request was accepted, an exact replay of it was answered 4.01, a re-encrypted message reusing the same PIV was rejected, a fresh PIV was accepted, and an unseen older PIV inside the window was accepted while a seen one was not; PIVs >= 2^40-1 are rejected. Encryption failures roll the window back (the shipped t_oscore_short_ciphertext_rollback test also covers this). No way found for an attacker without the master secret to advance or poison the window, since every state change is gated by a successful AEAD check or is rolled back."
          },
          "locations": [
