            "text": "Memory safety in pre-authentication parsing (OSCORE option, COSE, CBOR, plaintext/ciphertext length mismatch) — No issue identified: src/coap_oscore.c coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu (request + response paths, inner PDU assembly)\n\nTwo custom in-process harnesses fed coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu(): (a) 3,000,000 randomized OSCORE options (0-255 bytes, valid-ish first bytes, PIV/kid/kid_context permutations) with random ciphertext under ASAN+UBSAN, no report and stable RSS; (b) 30,000 iterations of *validly encrypted* messages (RFC keys, correct nonce/AAD, random inner plaintext including well-formed option streams with extended delta/length, Block/Observe/Uri-Path options and payloads) to exercise the post-decrypt inner-PDU copy path, no report. Also 400k randomized kid_context/PIV permutations with RFC 8613 Appendix B.2 enabled. Manual review of the ciphertext/plaintext length arithmetic (encrypt_len, tag_len, coap_pdu_init/resize sizing, plain_pdu->used_size) found the added `encrypt_len <= tag_len` guard prevents the previous empty-plaintext case. Outstanding anomalies from this surface are tracked in the B.2 and external-credential reports."
