        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/length-truncation-unauthenticated-option-content-influencing-oscore-state",
          "ruleIndex": 44,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Length truncation / unauthenticated option content influencing OSCORE state — Ruled out: src/coap_pdu.c OSCORE option length validation vs coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu osc_size (uint8_t)\n\ncoap_pdu_parse_opt() calls coap_pdu_parse_opt_base() for every parsed option, which rejects COAP_OPTION_OSCORE with len > 255 (src/coap_pdu.c:1343); coap_handle_dgram() then treats the PDU as malformed and answers 4.02 Bad Option without ever calling coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu(), so the `uint8_t osc_size = coap_opt_length(opt)` truncation in coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu() cannot be reached with a >255-byte option. Verified with a live server: a 258-byte OSCORE option is answered 4.02 and no OSCORE processing/log line is produced. Inside the decoder, option_len > 255, partial_iv_len 6/7, reserved bits and offset+kid_context.length > option_len are all rejected, so the kid/piv slices stay inside the option."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
