            "text": "Memory safety in config parsing (line splitting, hex decoding, keyword tables) — No issue identified: src/coap_oscore.c coap_parse_oscore_conf_mem / get_split_entry / parse_hex_bin (OSCORE config text parser)\n\nReviewed get_split_entry(), parse_hex_bin(), the oscore_config[] tables and coap_parse_oscore_conf_mem(); every memchr/strlen count is bounded by the remaining line/buffer length, parse_hex_bin allocates (end-begin)/2 and consumes exactly two hex digits per output byte, ids > 7 bytes are rejected, and duplicate keywords are refused. Fuzzed coap_new_oscore_conf() with a seed corpus of all documented keywords plus random mutation (insert/delete/byte-flip/quote/escape/newline, ~200k inputs) under ASAN+UBSAN together with oscore_decode_option_value: no sanitizer report. Input is operator-supplied configuration, not network-reachable."
