        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/pre-auth-cbor-parsing-recursion-depth-unchecked-lengths",
          "ruleIndex": 46,
          "kind": "notApplicable",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Pre-auth CBOR parsing / recursion depth / unchecked lengths — Not applicable: src/coap_subscribe.c coap_persist_observe_add OSCORE association blob (oscore_info) parsing\n\nThe CBOR parser is only used on data the application itself persisted (the association blob written by coap_add_observer and handed back through the observe-persist callback), not on network input, so an unauthenticated peer cannot supply it. Reviewed anyway: every byte-string length is compared against the remaining buffer before the slice is taken and before the pointer is advanced, and the array count is checked to be 5. Note two quirks worth knowing (no memory-safety impact): the nil case is compared with `oscore_cbor_get_element_size(...) == CBOR_NULL`, which can never be true because get_element_size returns the simple-value byte (0x16 for nil) rather than CBOR_NULL, and oscore_cbor_skip_value/strip_value (only used by unit tests) recurse without a depth limit — not reachable from this path."
          },
          "locations": [
