        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/heap-buffer-overflow-undersized-allocation-in-path-assembly",
          "ruleIndex": 49,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Heap buffer overflow / undersized allocation in path assembly — Ruled out: src/coap_uri.c:1204-1291 coap_get_uri_path() (Uri-Path loop, Uri-Path-Abbrev and Proxy-Uri branches)\n\nUri-Path loop: pass 1 (lines 1252-1265) adds sum(enc(seg_i)) + n then subtracts 1; pass 2 (lines 1273-1288) writes exactly (n-1) '/' separators plus sum(enc), same predicate, same iterator, same uint16_t truncation of coap_opt_length(), and uri_path->length is set to the same value, so writes == length and coap_new_string() zero-terminates at s[length]. Uri-Path-Abbrev branch (1213-1233) sizes with strlen(exp) and memcpy's exactly strlen(exp) (coap_new_string already stores the length). Proxy-Uri branch (1235-1249) sizes with uri.path.length, which coap_split_uri_sub derives from bounds already checked against the option length (src/coap_uri.c:315-341), and memcpy's exactly that many bytes. Verified under ASAN+UBSAN: h1.c (all path cases above incl. 1500 segments and 1000x255 all-'%'), h3.c (abbrev mappings of 1/5/64/255/1024/4096 bytes, unknown abbrev -> NULL, abbrev+Uri-Path -> NULL, 15 Proxy-Uri variants incl. a 1000-byte path, empty path, IPv6 host, '?'), h4.c (2983 randomized cases) - 0 failures, no sanitizer output. Over-cap (>255) segments are unreachable: src/coap_pdu.c:1336-1341 rejects them at parse, add, insert, update and optlist time."
          },
          "locations": [
