        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/heap-buffer-overflow-from-two-pass-length-write-mismatch",
          "ruleIndex": 50,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Heap buffer overflow from two-pass length/write mismatch — Ruled out: src/coap_uri.c:1110-1174 coap_get_query()\n\nNamed control: both passes are provably the same function of the same inputs. Pass 1 (lines 1123-1136) computes length = sum(enc(seg_i)) + n, then subtracts exactly 1, i.e. sum(enc) + (n-1); pass 2 (lines 1150-1170) writes one '&' for every option except the first ((n-1) separators) plus sum(enc), using the same is_unescaped_in_query() predicate, the same iterator/filter, and the same `uint16_t seg_len = coap_opt_length(q)` truncation. coap_new_string() (src/coap_str.c:21-47) allocates size+1 and sets s[size]=0, so the buffer is exactly length+1. Verified with ASAN+UBSAN builds (clang -fsanitize=address,undefined) against build-asan/libcoap-3.a: 229 authored cases (/workspace/uria/h1.c) over lengths 0,1,2,3,63,127,254,255 with byte classes '%','&','=','/',0x00,0x7f,0x80,0xff,'A' and mixed soup, 1/2/3/17/300/1500 repeated options with leading/middle/trailing empty options, 1000x255 all-'%' and 200x255 all-'&', plus 2983 randomized differential cases (/workspace/uria/h4.c) comparing length, full content and s[length]==NUL against an independently written encoder: 0 failures, no sanitizer output. Over-length values (256/1000/60000) are rejected by coap_add_option at src/coap_pdu.c:872 via the per-option cap at src/coap_pdu.c:1359-1362."
          },
