          "message": {
            "text": "NULL dereference in callers due to NULL-on-absent-option semantics — Ruled out: coap_get_query() NULL-on-no-Uri-Query behaviour change\n\ncoap_get_query() now returns NULL when no Uri-Query option exists (src/coap_uri.c:1137-1144), whereas upstream returned a zero-length string, so every library consumer was checked for a NULL dereference: src/coap_net.c:4215 (only forwarded to the app handler), src/coap_resource.c:1088-1099 (all uses are `uri_query ? ... : ...` ternaries and coap_delete_string(NULL) is safe), src/coap_resource.c:1326 and :1426, src/coap_subscribe.c:1001 (forwarded to handler), src/coap_proxy.c:923 and :1463 (passed to coap_add_data_large_response_lkd, which guards with `query ? query : &empty` at src/coap_block.c:788-790 and :2691, and copies under `if (query)` at :1219). No unguarded dereference exists; the change is a behaviour difference, not a crash. Exercised live: a no-query GET returns 2.05 from the ASAN example server over both UDP and TCP."
