          "message": {
            "text": "Remote memory corruption via attacker-supplied Uri-Path/Uri-Query options — No issue identified: Live coap-server UDP+TCP request path exercising coap_get_uri_path()/coap_get_query()\n\nLive ASAN+UBSAN build of examples/coap-server (build-asan) on 127.0.0.1:56831 with UDP and TCP endpoints, driven by hand-built CoAP PDUs (/workspace/uria/udp_test.py and tcp_test.py). UDP: valid /.well-known/core and /time?x=1 -> 2.05; 255-byte Uri-Path -> 4.04 (processed); 256-byte -> 4.02 with server log 'option 11 has bad length 256'; 60000-byte and 200x255 aggregate -> server log 'coap_pdu_resize: pdu too big' and the PDU is discarded. TCP: valid -> 2.05; 255-byte path -> 4.04; 256/60000/65804-byte Uri-Path -> 4.02; 256/60000/65804-byte Uri-Query -> 4.02; 200x255-byte Uri-Path (51 KB PDU) -> 4.04; 1000x255-byte all-'&' Uri-Query (257 KB PDU) -> 2.05, i.e. coap_get_query() really did assemble 1000 segments in-process. Server logs show only the expected cap/reject warnings; grep for AddressSanitizer/runtime error/SEGV returns 0 hits and the server stayed alive across all cases."
          },
